rder in Ireland and he is that  was a problem is the backstop is  different in this sense that the  backstop which the government's  negotiated we cannot get out of we are  handing over our sovereignty to the  European Union there's no  a natural way out of this for the  country that's good listen we want a  customs union tailor-made for ours which  will deliver proper jobs regional  development and a way forward out of  this crisis which protects jobs and also  respects the Good Friday Agreement in  Ireland that is a very important  achievement for our country the last 30  years we don't want to jeopardize it now  look the Chancellor himself is sitting  here in this very see a few moments ago  more or less dropping the deal we have  proposed an alternative set of  arrangements we think it's a reasonable  way forward but we're happy to negotiate  with others and Jeremy Corbyn is now  leading the conversations to try to find  a consensus the Chancellor also didn't  rule out the idea of a second referendum  if it meant for example tourism a still  passing and then having a public vote to  see if that would be acceptable to the  public and there was a million people  which holds marching yesterday in  support for a second referendum  why wasn't Tremec open there well he was  out campaigning a more commercially  where the cockle pickers died and what  the country wants to talk about for  instance crime was right and tried a  crime there were 20,000 less police  officers on the streets and this great  anxiety about the state of country apart  from Brazil and who is out there Jeremy  Jeremy is out there leading the country  discussing austerity and all the other  things that matter I was in London  yesterday I was in a series of meetings  but I took a bit of time I come had  conversations with people on the March  and what was interesting was there was  passion there was enthusiasm but above  all there was fear that this government  is simply lost and it's leading the  country down a blind alley into a very  very dangerous moment that was the  overwhelming impression I impression I  had it was a lovely crowd but the job of  a no to alternative government is try to  find a way of bringing all the sites  together in our country rather than  dividing it in the way that they thought  the government has on a brexit but a  bracelet which works for everybody I'm  interested to know your own views on  it's like I'm a friend and we spoke  about it the last time that you're on  the program can have a quick look  what you told us back then you said if  people feel that a privileged political  elite has decided to find a way of  reversing the previous referendum that  would cause us some difficulty and  rightly so is that what you think it is  what I think and from the beginning  there were some people who right from  the beginning didn't accept the results  of the referendum they wanted to remain  they want you to find a way of really  reversing the referendum the original  referendum that isn't Labour's position  our position is we've accepted the  results of the referendum but we think  we are now getting closer and closer to  a precipice and what we said is if we  arrive at a position where it's  necessary to prevent either a crash out  deal on or a dreadful Tory deal then at  that point we will seek to have a second  referendum by the way I am look I voted  for it labour put down a resolution as  it was in January which included a a  vote and by the way tomorrow we've got  another amendment which also includes a  second referendum but that's sorry how  would you vote if there was a referendum  I'd vote to remain and reform but we'd  have to see what other options were on  the table the truth is we are somewhere  away from making that decision look we  can spend a lot of time discussing  process how will we arrive at a decision  actually we should be discussing content  and the content is a deal which can work  which will deliver jobs and a more  prosperous country and we need to  reverse austerity and the problems which  our country's facing okay well let's  talk about the content shall we because  we just heard as well from the  Chancellor that the House of Commons  will have a opportunity to express its  view and try and find a majority around  something next week potentially through  this series of what's been known as  indicative votes so would you vote for  the Prime Minister's deal plus a customs  union as a compromise  no I think the Prime Minister's deal  simply didn't work and the main problem  we have is we've got a long term  relationship in a backs table from which  there is no exit and it's like  max Robb is a customs union but there is  no way out of it into a permanent  relationship we could be locked forever  into a situation which is something  short of what the people have voted for  and therefore we don't think that will  work  look we've made proposal it's got five  aspects to it and we are pushing it down  tomorrow night but equally our our  resolution tomorrow in front of the  House of Commons suggests that there are  a number of options which the house  should consider and I was pleased to see  the Chancellor of the Exchequer saying  actually he thinks that's what we're  going to end up look the point is mrs.  maid doesn't have the political skills  of negotiation and persuasion and charm  which is needed to win the majority of a  house where she doesn't have a majority  yourself and Jeremy is putting himself  in that position gradually emerging as a  national leader negotiating with Tories  with liberals with other parties trying  to find a way out of the message being  laid in so do you think a different  leader of the Conservative Party would  make it easier for Nate I think whatever  happens is in childhood for the Tory  party they've indeed led us into this  mess remember it was camera mr. camera  and mr. Osbourne that had the referendum  in the first place and tried to body the  country into a particular decision and I  think look the cabinet has made a mess  of this we need a general election  that's the kind of people's what we want  that's not sound like someone about to  do do with the concept we want to create  a consensus in the whole country part of  the problem is the government which has  lost its way okay John track it thank  you very much

